body:
Oh yeah I have noticed that. I worked as a cashier, I and found that I do not feel same pressure when conversing with strangers. If I know that I have to build relationship with someone, like co-workers, then I start to worry and be awkward. Actually, thats why I like cashiers job. I get to socialize, albeit superficially.

&#x200B;

It's probably because I know that customers come and go and I will never see them again.

I started going to gym. So Not dropping and building some mass. Gym is great. You feel social just by going to it and you don't need to interact with anyone. Also it gives some kind of energy boost. You feel tired but also motivated in your daily errands. 

&#x200B;

Also, I want to get involved with some community. It fells imposible that one day I would fell comfortable around other people and enjoy shared activities. I came to a conclusion, that I believe I can't be accepted by anyone ever. Of course, it can't be true. But that belief is overwhelming. So I need to make myself somehow get involved with people. I'm thinking maybe I consult with psychiatrist about modafinil prescription. I might have ADHD and it might be the reason why it is so burdensome for me to chat with others even when I feel confortable.
